[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table shows otherwise,
and the report text shows a third problem the table files away as a footnote.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, each with its own ticket. The queued parser fix closes only the first.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **parser:** the shared parser reads day-first dates month first. Every report that names both
  dates shows an exact day/month swap.
- **hint:** the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads what people typed day first.
  Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. A parser fix does not change the hint.
- **one-day:** the date moves by one day, and it depends on where the reader is ("Client in
  Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). These are the desk's one-day moves.
  `CauseTable` counts them under `parser` because of their tenant; a parser fix will not touch them.

## What #4471 shows today

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Why they were merged

Reports merge on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All three
problems arrive under the same subjects ("Date is wrong", "Month and day swapped?"), so
subject matching put them in one ticket. Intake's tag does not separate them either: it guesses
from the reporter's browser, and the cause depends on the tenant and the way in.

